WEBVTT

1
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:11,520
[♪ tense music playing]

2
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:14,160
- [parent 1 screams] Ow!
- [parent 2] Oh!

3
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:18,520
What about Mom?

4
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,000
She will come, too.

5
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:22,360
My husband abducted my child!

6
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:23,680
{\an8}AXIVORA

7
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:27,840
[ship horn blowing]

8
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:49,600
A kid, about five years old,
abducted by a man.

9
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:52,000
It might be the father.

10
00:00:52,080 --> 00:00:55,360
Um... A gray car. Number plate...

11
00:00:56,560 --> 00:00:58,360
Freeway

12
00:00:58,440 --> 00:00:59,640
An airport...

13
00:01:00,200 --> 00:01:01,200
Germany...

14
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:10,760
[passengers chattering]

15
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:30,440
[ship horn blows]

16
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:37,880
the last scene

17
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:41,400
Hayal! You called.

18
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:42,640
I'm on my way.

19
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:44,400
[Hayal] <i>Waiting. Come on.</i>

20
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:45,480
Okay.

21
00:01:48,960 --> 00:01:49,960
[sighs]

22
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:57,720
[Hayal] <i>...consider it as a synopsis.
Two pages.</i>

23
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,200
Consider it as a synopsis.

24
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:02,120
<i>I've already started on the script.
I'll deliver it as soon as it's ready.</i>

25
00:02:02,200 --> 00:02:03,680
I'll... I'll deliver it
as soon as it's ready.

26
00:02:03,760 --> 00:02:06,760
<i>I also want to thank you specifically
for giving me this opportunity.</i>

27
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:09,440
I also want to thank you
for giving me this opportunity.

28
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:14,400
[♪ tense music playing]

29
00:02:43,560 --> 00:02:44,560
Selen!

30
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:49,480
The wilding is here.

31
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:51,600
Don't worry, she's the best at her job.

32
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,920
The top name in drama.

33
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:56,360
I've seen her take the script to
a whole new level with just one sentence.

34
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:59,000
She keeps talking about
a story she's working on,

35
00:02:59,080 --> 00:03:01,280
but no one has read a line yet.

36
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,440
[parent 2] Welcome.

37
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:13,120
- Have I kept you waiting?
- Not at all, dear.

38
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:14,560
Come, sit down.

39
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:17,280
I need to head to the set,
which is why I called you.

40
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:18,560
Let me introduce you.

41
00:03:18,640 --> 00:03:21,040
- Doruk, Selen. Selen, Doruk.
- Hi.

42
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:22,240
- What's up?
- Hello.

43
00:03:22,800 --> 00:03:25,280
Doruk could be our next screenwriter.

44
00:03:25,360 --> 00:03:26,920
He has a story I read and loved.

45
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,480
He's never written
for the screen before, though.

46
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,120
You should work on it together.

47
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:35,440
Just give him some pointers.
Doruk will sort out the rest.

48
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:36,520
Give her the synopsis.

49
00:03:36,600 --> 00:03:37,760
Of course.

50
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,360
[Selen clears throat]

51
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:52,320
I'll take a look.

52
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:55,080
- Do that.
- [phone ringing]

53
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:57,120
[Doruk] Ladies, please excuse me.

54
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:58,960
I need to take this.

55
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:00,040
Go ahead.

56
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:10,280
Deal with this, okay?

57
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:11,360
What about your script?

58
00:04:11,440 --> 00:04:12,920
Send it over sometime
so I can take a look.

59
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:16,120
- [parent 1] Ow!
- [server] I'm so sorry.

60
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:18,840
[parent 1] What do you think
you're doing? [speaks indistinctly]

61
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:20,320
- It was an accident. Wait.
- Oh, it's ruined!

62
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:22,880
Pfft! Okay, okay.
I'll go and get it cleaned.

63
00:04:22,960 --> 00:04:24,960
[♪ tense music playing]

64
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:27,720
Ow!

65
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:35,160
Come with me.

66
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,880
I have a terrific surprise for you.

67
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:42,200
I should be going.
Um... I've got the script.

68
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:44,560
I'll read it and get back to you
in the morning, okay?

69
00:04:44,640 --> 00:04:46,240
You can't just leave.

70
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:53,360
[parent 2] Hop into the car.

71
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:55,600
- In you go.
- [child] What about mom?

72
00:04:58,160 --> 00:04:59,160
I don't know.

73
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:01,480
He left with your son
the moment you went in.

74
00:05:01,560 --> 00:05:03,040
- Where would they go?
- I don't know.

75
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:05,360
We're going through a divorce,
but he wouldn't do something like this.

76
00:05:05,440 --> 00:05:08,000
- Then where could they have gone?
- I don't know.

77
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:10,200
Murat! Murat!

78
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:12,160
Murat! Wait!

79
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:15,000
So... Um... [mumbles] Airport...

80
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:16,080
Is that possible?

81
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:19,200
Because I think he said
something like Germany.

82
00:05:19,280 --> 00:05:22,480
- Hmm?
- [mumbles] Taxi!

83
00:05:22,560 --> 00:05:24,560
Taxi! Taxi!

84
00:05:25,200 --> 00:05:26,760
I'd like to report an incident.

85
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:28,400
A child abduction. Um...

86
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:31,800
They're heading to
Istanbul Airport from Sariyer.

87
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:36,360
Um, the number plate...

88
00:05:36,440 --> 00:05:37,640
34... N...

89
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:40,720
POLICE

90
00:05:45,680 --> 00:05:46,920
Sir, could I see some ID?

91
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,480
Certainly, officer. What's this about?

92
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:51,480
Is there a problem?

93
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:58,000
A complaint was filed against you.
Can you please step out of the vehicle?

94
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:59,400
A complaint... Now...

95
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:01,880
Could there be a mistake, Mr. Officer?

96
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:04,480
There's nothing to justify a complaint.

97
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:08,760
- There they are.
- Stop.

98
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:10,480
Please, stop!

99
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:14,680
Murat! Murat, stop!

100
00:06:14,760 --> 00:06:16,040
He abducted my child! My son!

101
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:19,560
- Mine, dear, what are you doing? Mine?
- Oh, my boy. [speaks indistinctly]

102
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:22,360
Mr. Officer, this man is trying to
take the child from his mother.

103
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:24,480
Oh, no. That is totally untrue!

104
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:25,760
He's lying, Mr. Officer!

105
00:06:25,840 --> 00:06:28,240
- He abducted the child!
- Who are you anyway?

106
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:29,480
You're lying!

107
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:31,000
Who are you?

108
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:39,480
[groans]

109
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:44,520
[♪ eerie music playing]

110
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,000
[sighs]

111
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:57,720
[breathes deeply]

112
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:04,920
JUNE
Saved child

113
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,400
Kid saved.

114
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:15,800
Brawl and stabbing at
supermarket - Mert makes up

115
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:19,200
Assault at wedding - Stabbing
Motorbike accident

116
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:20,680
Sexual assault
Name is Ceyda

117
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:21,760
Admission of wrong project

118
00:07:21,840 --> 00:07:23,240
Ferry malfunction
collision - PREVENTED

119
00:07:54,440 --> 00:07:55,760
[sighs]

120
00:07:55,840 --> 00:07:57,080
SPIRAL OF SILENCE
SELEN KAYA

121
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,920
You failed to deliver your script again.

122
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,000
You're hopeless, Selen.

123
00:08:26,280 --> 00:08:27,520
[gasps]

124
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:28,760
[groans]

125
00:08:30,200 --> 00:08:31,200
[huffs]

126
00:08:32,560 --> 00:08:33,560
[sighs]

127
00:08:34,840 --> 00:08:35,840
[sighs deeply]

128
00:08:46,160 --> 00:08:47,840
[breathes deeply]

129
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:02,360
[♪ upbeat music playing]

130
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:13,000
[crowd] Ten, nine, eight,

131
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:16,520
seven, six, five, four,

132
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:19,200
three, two, one!

133
00:09:19,280 --> 00:09:21,280
[screaming, cheering]

134
00:09:28,120 --> 00:09:29,560
WELCOME
2026

135
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:31,360
[tires screech]

136
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:33,480
[crowd clamoring]

137
00:09:33,560 --> 00:09:36,760
[witness] Oh! A car hit the woman!

138
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:38,760
[♪ dramatic music playing]

139
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:49,120
Hey... Look at me!

140
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:50,400
Can you hear me?

141
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:53,640
Stop staring, call an ambulance!

142
00:09:53,720 --> 00:09:55,400
- Come on!
- [witness 2] Call an ambulance!

143
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:57,160
It's on its way!
An ambulance is coming, okay?

144
00:09:57,240 --> 00:09:58,440
Hang in there a little longer!

145
00:09:58,520 --> 00:10:00,040
Don't die! Don't die! Let's see.

146
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:01,200
Fuck!

147
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,000
[panting]

148
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:11,240
- No! No, no, no!
- [exhales shakily]

149
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:25,120
[exhales sharply]

150
00:10:26,880 --> 00:10:28,320
[sniffles, exhales sharply]

151
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:33,840
[♪ dramatic music playing]

152
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:36,960
[Selen] <i>The first time...</i> [gasps]

153
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:38,040
DECEMBER 31

154
00:10:38,120 --> 00:10:41,840
<i>I'm seeing myself
in my dream for the first time.</i>

155
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:44,200
2025
198 DAYS

156
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:45,280
[gasps]

157
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:52,800
198 days to go.

158
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:56,280
In 198 days... [sighs]

159
00:10:56,920 --> 00:10:58,640
New Year's Eve.

160
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:01,120
- Past midnight...
- [tires squeal]

161
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:03,360
A car...

162
00:11:04,560 --> 00:11:07,320
An accident... Number plate... [sighs]

163
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,000
34 L...

164
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:11,680
[sighs] 34 L...

165
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:15,160
Six.

166
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:16,600
The first digit was six.

167
00:11:16,680 --> 00:11:18,520
I don't remember the rest.

168
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:20,040
[sighs] I must find the car.

169
00:11:20,120 --> 00:11:21,400
I must find the street.

170
00:11:21,480 --> 00:11:22,920
[sighs]

171
00:11:23,480 --> 00:11:24,800
This isn't the street!

172
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:26,960
It's not nearby. It's somewhere else.

173
00:11:27,040 --> 00:11:28,120
Where am I?

174
00:11:28,200 --> 00:11:30,440
Why am I there? What am I doing there?

175
00:11:30,520 --> 00:11:31,880
A dark red car.

176
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:32,960
A classic model.

177
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:36,120
The guy who helped me knew CPR.

178
00:11:36,200 --> 00:11:38,040
He might hold all the clues.

179
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:39,800
I must find him.

180
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:40,960
Find the guy.

181
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,840
Find the car. Find the street.

182
00:11:42,920 --> 00:11:45,400
[sighs, breathes heavily]

183
00:11:47,920 --> 00:11:49,480
I must prevent this.

184
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:54,640
I must save myself,
just like I do for everyone else.

185
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,400
[phone beeps, buzzes]

186
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:07,120
[Hayal] <i>Did you get my message?</i>

187
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:10,160
[stammers] Um, I did, yes.

188
00:12:10,240 --> 00:12:12,160
[Hayal] <i>You could
at least let me know, respond.</i>

189
00:12:12,240 --> 00:12:15,000
<i>I'm on set. Doruk is with me.</i>

190
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:17,120
<i>I'm sending my location.
Get over here, quick.</i>

191
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,320
[stammers] Okay.

192
00:12:18,960 --> 00:12:20,800
[sighs heavily]

193
00:12:24,880 --> 00:12:25,880
[sniffles]

194
00:12:25,960 --> 00:12:27,960
[♪ dramatic music playing]

195
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:36,680
2025
198 DAYS

196
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:40,800
[crew member] Come on, guys!

197
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:42,520
We start shooting in five! Come on!

198
00:12:43,240 --> 00:12:44,800
AMBULANCE
EMERGENCY SERVICE

199
00:12:48,360 --> 00:12:49,600
Spin, man!

200
00:12:54,680 --> 00:12:55,680
[speaks indistinctly]

201
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:58,440
Spin around! Good!

202
00:13:02,840 --> 00:13:03,840
[speaks indistinctly]

203
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:08,680
[crew member 2] Kemal! Wait, wait, wait!

204
00:13:08,760 --> 00:13:09,920
[speaks indistinctly]

205
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,720
Have you seen Hayal?

206
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:13,520
Hayal is with the director.

207
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:16,680
- [Selen sighs]
- Um, I think there's a problem.

208
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:18,120
They're in a meeting.

209
00:13:20,960 --> 00:13:23,600
So, did you read my story?

210
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:26,040
- [sighs]
- It was so short.

211
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:28,920
Yes.

212
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,480
I didn't read the short version, but...

213
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:32,760
I did finish the long one.

214
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:33,840
AFTERNOON SUN

215
00:13:33,920 --> 00:13:35,400
I mean the book.

216
00:13:36,560 --> 00:13:38,240
What? I don't get it.

217
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:41,320
You know what this is called? Plagiarism.

218
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:44,360
What do you mean, um...

219
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:46,760
Is it like my story?
Is the book something like it?

220
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:49,760
There's no such thing as your story.

221
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:51,960
This story is by Resat Nuri Güntekin.

222
00:13:53,320 --> 00:13:55,640
I mean...
There could be similarities, right?

223
00:13:55,720 --> 00:13:57,480
I'm just saying, isn't it possible?

224
00:13:57,560 --> 00:14:00,320
No, because it's the same.

225
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:01,840
The guy in the book
is also a wounded soldier.

226
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:05,480
The doctors warn him
that getting excited could be fatal.

227
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:08,320
The guy falls in love with a girl.

228
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:11,320
He becomes intimate with her,
knowing he will die.

229
00:14:11,880 --> 00:14:14,200
I think you should go to Hayal
and confess in person.

230
00:14:14,280 --> 00:14:15,760
I have to do it myself otherwise.

231
00:14:15,840 --> 00:14:16,920
It's nothing personal.

232
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,200
I'm only doing my job.

233
00:14:27,880 --> 00:14:29,840
Collectable - good condition
Oldsmobile Dynam...

234
00:14:29,920 --> 00:14:31,680
Original restoration -
rare Oldsmobile 88...

235
00:14:44,040 --> 00:14:45,040
[Hayal] That bastard!

236
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:46,400
He thought he could get away with it.

237
00:14:46,480 --> 00:14:49,000
- I'm so pissed off. [clicks tongue]
- [Selen coughs]

238
00:14:49,080 --> 00:14:50,920
Well done, you. You don't miss a thing.

239
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,480
- Hmm!
- [crew member] Come on, guys!

240
00:14:52,560 --> 00:14:54,160
We start rolling in five minutes. Hurry!

241
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:56,360
- Come on, they're almost ready.
- Come over.

242
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:58,160
- Come with me.
- Ready in two minutes.

243
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,120
Right, let's roll.

244
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:03,680
I hope it turns out to be worth
all this expense and improves the ratings.

245
00:15:03,760 --> 00:15:05,280
Sure, it will.

246
00:15:05,360 --> 00:15:07,960
[crew member]
Guys, can we start shooting already?

247
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:10,640
- Hayal, can I go?
- Hold on. You'll go after this is over.

248
00:15:10,720 --> 00:15:11,800
Camera!

249
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:14,360
Three, two, one, action!

250
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:35,160
Cut! That's great!

251
00:15:35,800 --> 00:15:36,920
Keep the boat where it is.

252
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,280
Let's get him out the water.

253
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:39,680
Stop the boat.

254
00:15:39,760 --> 00:15:41,600
- [sighs]
- Can I go?

255
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:43,920
Wait, it won't be long.

256
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:46,120
[crew member 1] Can we get
Kemal out of the water, please?

257
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:47,840
[♪ dramatic music playing]

258
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:52,520
[crew member 2] He's not moving!

259
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:53,920
- What's wrong?
- Medic!

260
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:56,080
Help! Something's happened to him!

261
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:58,240
- Over here!
- Is he okay?

262
00:15:58,320 --> 00:15:59,480
I don't know.

263
00:16:00,360 --> 00:16:02,800
- [crew member 4] Here.
- Paramedic! Have you sent for a paramedic?

264
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:05,120
[crew member 1]
Time to get him out, paramedics.

265
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:16,960
- Whoo-hoo!
- [crew members cheering]

266
00:16:17,040 --> 00:16:18,360
[no audible dialogue]

267
00:16:19,920 --> 00:16:20,920
[Kemal] Dude!

268
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,600
The water is so nice.

269
00:16:22,680 --> 00:16:23,680
Jump in!

270
00:16:23,760 --> 00:16:25,200
Some joke.

271
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:26,760
Who is he?

272
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:27,840
Seriously?

273
00:16:27,920 --> 00:16:29,920
We've been shooting for three months.

274
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,800
He's Emirhan's double.

275
00:16:31,880 --> 00:16:34,320
He also choreographs our fight scenes.

276
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:37,000
- Kemal.
- [crew member] Come here, man. Here.

277
00:16:37,800 --> 00:16:40,880
- It was a joke, Selçuk. All good.
- [Selçuk] All right.

278
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:42,920
[crew member 4] Man. [speaks indistinctly]

279
00:16:45,680 --> 00:16:47,280
- You'll kill yourself one day. Seriously.
- I'll be fine.

280
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:49,080
- I'll be fine. I'm fine.
- You're okay, right?

281
00:16:49,160 --> 00:16:51,440
[crew member 5]
Okay, guys, everyone to the caravans!

282
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:54,240
[♪ dramatic music playing]

283
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,120
Thank you.

284
00:17:17,120 --> 00:17:18,680
Berk, which vehicle is leaving?

285
00:17:18,760 --> 00:17:20,520
- Cengiz is going.
- [Kemal] Thanks.

286
00:17:20,600 --> 00:17:22,680
- That was some jump, man. Way to go.
- Thanks, I appreciate it.

287
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:24,640
I double my fee
for anything over 15 meters.

288
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:26,240
- Remember that.
- [Berk] Will do.

289
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:28,880
Cengo, old timer!

290
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:30,240
You'll drop me off
at the park down the road, won't you?

291
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:32,280
- [Cengiz] Hop in, man!
- [Kemal] You're the man!

292
00:17:47,960 --> 00:17:50,680
kemalsezer_
Follow

293
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:58,040
[Kemal] <i>Aytug!</i>

294
00:17:58,120 --> 00:17:59,760
<i>The key is in the caravan.</i>

295
00:18:00,760 --> 00:18:02,240
<i>I'll bring it, I'll bring it.
Hold on. Wait.</i>

296
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:04,680
[♪ dramatic music playing]

297
00:18:06,720 --> 00:18:08,880
[Kemal] Cengiz, leave me here, will you?

298
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:09,960
[Cengiz] Sure thing.

299
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:13,080
[Kemal] Thanks. Take it easy, man.

300
00:18:13,160 --> 00:18:14,640
[Cengiz] Thanks, man. Later.

301
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:23,080
Are you following me?

302
00:18:25,120 --> 00:18:26,160
No.

303
00:18:28,040 --> 00:18:29,480
Excuse me.

304
00:18:29,560 --> 00:18:31,200
Actually... Um...

305
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:34,160
It's not like stalking, but...

306
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:38,680
Um... I'm with the production company.

307
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,440
I know, Selen.

308
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:43,440
How... How do you know my name?

309
00:18:43,520 --> 00:18:45,840
[chuckles] We work at the same company.

310
00:18:45,920 --> 00:18:47,360
Could that be why?

311
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:50,520
Right. Um...

312
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:55,120
The thing is, my boss wants to learn
a few things about you.

313
00:18:56,280 --> 00:18:57,680
Like what?

314
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:59,880
Where do you live? Your street.

315
00:18:59,960 --> 00:19:02,520
Do you know CPR?

316
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:04,240
I mean, can you do it?

317
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:06,480
- [snaps fingers]
- New Year's Eve. Um...

318
00:19:06,560 --> 00:19:08,720
Where do you plan to celebrate? [chuckles]

319
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:12,040
Okay, you're right.

320
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,600
Let's go one by one.

321
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:14,680
Do you have a driver's license?

322
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:16,440
Are you crazy? Of course.

323
00:19:16,520 --> 00:19:18,960
Okay. Do you own a car?

324
00:19:19,040 --> 00:19:20,440
What's the number plate?

325
00:19:20,520 --> 00:19:22,960
I don't own a car,
so there's no number plate.

326
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:24,360
Are you planning to buy one?

327
00:19:25,360 --> 00:19:27,680
There are a couple of models
I've set my eyes on.

328
00:19:27,760 --> 00:19:29,400
[laughs] What's this about?

329
00:19:29,480 --> 00:19:31,480
Am I getting a company car?

330
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:35,240
Well, I'm not sure.
You know the boss. [stammers]

331
00:19:35,320 --> 00:19:37,680
- The boss.
- He wanted to know.

332
00:19:38,880 --> 00:19:40,240
Any more questions?

333
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,240
[sighs]

334
00:19:42,320 --> 00:19:43,440
Actually, there is, but...

335
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:46,200
- Hold on.
- Good. Come with me.

336
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:47,760
Oh! What are you doing?

337
00:19:47,840 --> 00:19:49,600
Hold on! What are you doing?

338
00:19:49,680 --> 00:19:50,960
Listen to me. I...

339
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:53,000
I don't like this sort of stuff.

340
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:54,720
Please let go of me.

341
00:19:54,800 --> 00:19:56,080
Ugh!

342
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:58,880
[breathing shakily]

343
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:02,480
I almost got killed!

344
00:20:03,320 --> 00:20:05,360
Do you think I'd let that happen?

345
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:07,240
- Never.
- [exhales sharply]

346
00:20:18,080 --> 00:20:19,080
I'm sorry.

347
00:20:20,120 --> 00:20:21,320
I scared you. Okay.

348
00:20:22,840 --> 00:20:24,440
Let me do something to make it up to you.

349
00:20:25,120 --> 00:20:26,160
Let me buy you lunch.

350
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:28,280
Or a coffee.

351
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:29,360
Coffee?

352
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:33,960
Am I supposed to get on this?

353
00:20:34,040 --> 00:20:35,920
- After that reckless crossing.
- [laughs]

354
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,240
You won't find anyone better than me.

355
00:20:38,320 --> 00:20:39,680
You must have noticed at the set.

356
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:42,360
Yes, I did. I saw you plunge into the sea.

357
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:44,360
Well, I was following the script.

358
00:20:44,960 --> 00:20:46,280
Listen, we're out in the sun.

359
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:47,560
You're out of water.

360
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:49,520
I'll answer all your questions.

361
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:50,960
Everything. In full.

362
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:54,160
Come on.

363
00:20:56,800 --> 00:20:57,800
The boss!

364
00:21:01,120 --> 00:21:02,520
You coming?

365
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:03,600
Or should I go?

366
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:06,880
[♪ funky music playing]

367
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:10,960
You stick to the rules
and ride responsibly.

368
00:21:11,040 --> 00:21:12,040
Deal.

369
00:21:14,560 --> 00:21:15,560
[sighs]

370
00:21:17,480 --> 00:21:19,080
No speeding, either.

371
00:21:19,840 --> 00:21:20,920
Agreed.

372
00:21:21,680 --> 00:21:23,680
[screams]

373
00:21:25,280 --> 00:21:26,800
Is this what you call slow?

374
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:27,960
Is this slow?

375
00:21:29,880 --> 00:21:32,720
- What did you say?
- Is this supposed to be slow?

376
00:21:32,800 --> 00:21:35,000
Ugh!

377
00:21:35,840 --> 00:21:38,000
I can't go any slower on this road.

378
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:40,400
But you promised me.

379
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:42,560
You said you'd go slow. Ugh!

380
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:44,720
Can you leave me here?

381
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:46,000
Can I get off?

382
00:21:46,080 --> 00:21:48,000
Can you stop now?

383
00:21:48,080 --> 00:21:49,440
I want to get off!

384
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:51,360
Please stop, please stop!

385
00:21:51,440 --> 00:21:53,200
I don't want to die!

386
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:55,960
[screams]

387
00:21:57,080 --> 00:21:58,200
How's this?

388
00:21:58,280 --> 00:22:00,800
[screams] Ha-ha-ha!

389
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:02,160
Amazing!

390
00:22:02,240 --> 00:22:04,400
Go a little slower! Slow!

391
00:22:15,440 --> 00:22:17,360
Where is this place you talked about?

392
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:18,440
So?

393
00:22:19,160 --> 00:22:20,160
Oh!

394
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:22,520
What are you doing? What are you doing?

395
00:22:22,600 --> 00:22:25,000
Can you get down? Down! Down! Down! Oh!

396
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:26,080
I can't even look. Please.

397
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:27,680
What are you doing?

398
00:22:27,760 --> 00:22:28,840
Come over.

399
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:31,360
Never! Why would I? Why?

400
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:32,680
Get down!

401
00:22:34,880 --> 00:22:38,040
To take in and enjoy the scenery.

402
00:22:38,600 --> 00:22:40,680
Oh, oh! But... But...

403
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:41,920
What's your problem?

404
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:44,360
To feel the wind.

405
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:47,000
Please get down. Please.

406
00:22:47,080 --> 00:22:50,560
Listen, I really don't like
this sort of thing!

407
00:22:52,040 --> 00:22:53,400
Oh...

408
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:54,840
[gasps]

409
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:56,560
- [scoffs]
- Let me help you get closer slowly.

410
00:22:56,640 --> 00:22:58,920
- No way!
- You'll get used to it.

411
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:00,040
No. I don't want to.

412
00:23:00,120 --> 00:23:02,200
I didn't want to come up here
in the first place.

413
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:04,200
You can't ride elevators.

414
00:23:04,280 --> 00:23:05,640
You're afraid of heights.

415
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:07,280
You clearly have serious issues.

416
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:09,560
I urge you to confront them,
or you'll never get past it.

417
00:23:09,640 --> 00:23:10,640
It's impossible.

418
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:12,360
It's dangerous.

419
00:23:12,440 --> 00:23:13,440
End of story.

420
00:23:14,520 --> 00:23:16,160
Why are we even here?

421
00:23:16,240 --> 00:23:20,400
Because the answers
to many of your questions are here.

422
00:23:22,080 --> 00:23:24,200
I live in this building, right below.

423
00:23:25,240 --> 00:23:29,720
I'll also celebrate New Year's
on this terrace.

424
00:23:32,560 --> 00:23:34,800
Promise. It's safe. Honestly.

425
00:23:47,480 --> 00:23:49,680
Oh, I'm more dangerous
than heights, is that it?

426
00:23:51,920 --> 00:23:53,920
[♪ romantic music playing]

427
00:23:57,280 --> 00:24:00,920
I've waited three months
to see this smile up close.

428
00:24:02,120 --> 00:24:03,120
Three months?

429
00:24:04,320 --> 00:24:05,400
Three months.

430
00:24:10,080 --> 00:24:14,640
<i>You looked so peaceful and calm
amid that crowd, chaos, and scurry.</i>

431
00:24:15,800 --> 00:24:17,840
<i>It was impossible to miss.</i>

432
00:24:19,520 --> 00:24:21,520
[Selen] <i>I... never even noticed.</i>

433
00:24:22,680 --> 00:24:23,680
[Kemal] <i>I know.</i>

434
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:28,360
<i>Actually, I could have made an effort
to get your attention.</i>

435
00:24:29,560 --> 00:24:31,120
<i>But something held me back.</i>

436
00:24:36,400 --> 00:24:37,840
I think I was scared for the first time.

437
00:24:38,560 --> 00:24:42,200
I mean, I was scared of
that feeling growing inside me.

438
00:24:44,120 --> 00:24:47,200
But now I'm exactly where
I was scared of being.

439
00:24:48,120 --> 00:24:51,680
But then, poof! All my fears... [chuckles]

440
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:53,000
They suddenly disappeared.

441
00:24:53,080 --> 00:24:55,000
[♪ romantic music playing]

442
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:07,120
[Selen] Mmm.

443
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:09,800
Um, should I... Should I go?

444
00:25:11,800 --> 00:25:13,680
- So, all right, this is the address.
- Uh-huh.

445
00:25:13,760 --> 00:25:15,800
So the street is down there.

446
00:25:15,880 --> 00:25:17,200
Thing, um...

447
00:25:17,920 --> 00:25:19,640
The celebrations are here.

448
00:25:20,560 --> 00:25:22,440
So, okay. See you around.

449
00:25:22,520 --> 00:25:24,480
[♪ romantic music playing]

450
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:33,120
[no audible dialogue]

451
00:25:54,080 --> 00:25:55,280
[Selen] I found the guy.

452
00:25:55,960 --> 00:25:56,960
His name is Kemal.

453
00:25:57,720 --> 00:25:59,280
He doesn't have a car.
That's not the street.

454
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:00,360
Guy found
Name is Kemal

455
00:26:00,440 --> 00:26:02,440
[♪ sad music playing]

456
00:26:09,800 --> 00:26:11,080
[laptop chimes]

457
00:26:14,480 --> 00:26:17,480
kemal sezer

458
00:26:24,280 --> 00:26:26,280
[phone ringing]

459
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:34,520
- Hello.
- [hotel clerk] <i>Good evening.</i>

460
00:26:34,600 --> 00:26:35,880
<i>I'm calling from Ada Hotel.</i>

461
00:26:35,960 --> 00:26:37,000
<i>Is this Ms. Selen?</i>

462
00:26:37,080 --> 00:26:39,360
Hello there. I was expecting your call.

463
00:26:39,440 --> 00:26:42,040
[hotel clerk] <i>So, you asked about
availability for the New Year,</i>

464
00:26:42,120 --> 00:26:44,680
<i>arriving December 30th
and leaving January second.</i>

465
00:26:44,760 --> 00:26:46,400
- <i>Is that correct?</i>
- That's correct.

466
00:26:46,480 --> 00:26:48,280
[hotel clerk]
<i>We currently have availability.</i>

467
00:26:48,360 --> 00:26:49,400
<i>I'll send you a payment link,</i>

468
00:26:49,480 --> 00:26:52,480
<i>and your reservation will be confirmed
once payment is received.</i>

469
00:26:52,560 --> 00:26:54,640
<i>Is there anything else
I can assist you with?</i>

470
00:26:54,720 --> 00:26:55,800
<i>Does that work for you?</i>

471
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:56,880
I hope so.

472
00:26:56,960 --> 00:26:58,720
[hotel clerk] <i>Excuse me?</i>

473
00:26:58,800 --> 00:27:00,360
That's fine. Thank you.

474
00:27:00,440 --> 00:27:02,160
[hotel clerk] <i>Okay, then. Goodbye.</i>

475
00:27:04,960 --> 00:27:06,960
[♪ sad music playing]

476
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:08,960
[sighs]

477
00:27:27,920 --> 00:27:29,800
- Uh-oh.
- Morning.

478
00:27:33,920 --> 00:27:35,320
What brought you here? Work?

479
00:27:35,400 --> 00:27:38,800
No, I came to see you and bring you this.

480
00:27:41,080 --> 00:27:42,080
Thank you.

481
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:45,760
Oh, and I have this for your eczema, too.

482
00:27:45,840 --> 00:27:48,920
It's a special cream I got
from an herbalist.

483
00:27:49,000 --> 00:27:50,200
It smells amazing.

484
00:27:50,280 --> 00:27:52,480
The guy told me that applying it
twice a day would be enough.

485
00:27:52,560 --> 00:27:54,520
And you shouldn't scratch these areas.

486
00:27:56,240 --> 00:27:57,960
You know it's
all related to stress, right?

487
00:27:58,040 --> 00:28:00,280
And digestion is important too.

488
00:28:00,360 --> 00:28:03,760
When you think about it,
the gut is where many diseases start.

489
00:28:03,840 --> 00:28:05,320
Is that so, Mr. Doc?

490
00:28:05,400 --> 00:28:07,720
No, I never finished.

491
00:28:07,800 --> 00:28:10,600
Oh! Seriously? Why?

492
00:28:10,680 --> 00:28:13,240
It wasn't a degree I could finish anyway.

493
00:28:14,240 --> 00:28:17,440
But, to answer your question,
I can do CPR.

494
00:28:19,280 --> 00:28:20,440
Good.

495
00:28:24,280 --> 00:28:25,280
Can I ask you something?

496
00:28:25,360 --> 00:28:26,640
Did you write this?

497
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:30,000
Since your name is on it,
it must be your work.

498
00:28:30,080 --> 00:28:31,080
What's happening to the girl?

499
00:28:31,160 --> 00:28:33,680
What was her name? Kavin. Kavin.

500
00:28:34,240 --> 00:28:36,120
I hope she doesn't freeze to death.

501
00:28:36,200 --> 00:28:39,800
What really upset me is
that the mother knows but remains silent,

502
00:28:39,880 --> 00:28:41,200
and the father is no different.

503
00:28:41,280 --> 00:28:42,600
He doesn't even believe his daughter.

504
00:28:42,680 --> 00:28:46,920
They could ask the uncle what he did
to her and why he laid a hand on her.

505
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:49,800
For example,
how many days does she stay in the stable?

506
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:53,720
Why did you read it
without asking me first?

507
00:28:53,800 --> 00:28:55,680
How could you do that?

508
00:28:57,520 --> 00:28:58,520
I...

509
00:28:59,480 --> 00:29:00,840
I didn't mean any harm.

510
00:29:00,920 --> 00:29:02,000
Honestly, I...

511
00:29:03,120 --> 00:29:05,680
It was there in the open. I took a look.

512
00:29:06,600 --> 00:29:07,600
Okay, I apologize.

513
00:29:07,680 --> 00:29:09,720
My bad. Again.

514
00:29:15,080 --> 00:29:16,720
[sighs] Does she die?

515
00:29:16,800 --> 00:29:18,120
Tell me that at least.

516
00:29:23,520 --> 00:29:24,600
No, she doesn't.

517
00:29:26,280 --> 00:29:27,760
[♪ sad music playing]

518
00:29:27,840 --> 00:29:28,840
[breathes deeply]

519
00:29:28,920 --> 00:29:32,200
She spends 28 days in the stable,
up in the hayloft.

520
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:34,480
It's a tiny, cramped space.

521
00:29:34,560 --> 00:29:35,960
No place to lie down, nothing.

522
00:29:36,040 --> 00:29:37,520
Just think about that.

523
00:29:37,600 --> 00:29:41,240
And yes, no one questions the uncle
about what he did to the girl.

524
00:29:41,320 --> 00:29:45,760
Meanwhile,
the father pressures the girl to lie.

525
00:29:46,360 --> 00:29:49,760
But Kavin says nothing. Hmm.

526
00:29:49,840 --> 00:29:52,360
[sighs] They then take her
to a teacher to cleanse her.

527
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:54,920
You know, spells and such.

528
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:56,440
Then...

529
00:29:56,520 --> 00:29:58,160
The parents conclude
there is no improvement,

530
00:29:58,240 --> 00:30:00,520
so they arrange for her to marry
one of the oldest men in the village.

531
00:30:00,600 --> 00:30:01,720
That's how it ends.

532
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:03,280
Seriously?

533
00:30:03,360 --> 00:30:04,640
She marries an old man?

534
00:30:05,240 --> 00:30:07,840
It's just something written
for no real reason. Nothing important.

535
00:30:07,920 --> 00:30:09,200
No, no.

536
00:30:09,840 --> 00:30:11,360
I think it's pretty impressive.

537
00:30:11,440 --> 00:30:13,320
I mean, it's dark and compelling.

538
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:15,000
Really.

539
00:30:17,400 --> 00:30:21,080
I've been waiting for months for a chance,
but Hayal keeps sidetracking me.

540
00:30:21,760 --> 00:30:25,920
All she says is,
"Finish writing, and we'll take a look."

541
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:28,520
She wastes my time with chores.

542
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:33,520
I mean...
They probably only see me as a playwright.

543
00:30:33,600 --> 00:30:34,840
Nothing else.

544
00:30:34,920 --> 00:30:36,400
Anyway, I quit writing.

545
00:30:36,480 --> 00:30:37,640
I no longer write.

546
00:30:39,200 --> 00:30:40,440
Do you always give up?

547
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:51,000
Hello?

548
00:30:51,080 --> 00:30:52,720
[caller] <i>I might have found that car.</i>

549
00:30:52,800 --> 00:30:53,840
<i>Come, take a look.</i>

550
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:55,680
Okay, I'm on my way.

551
00:30:55,760 --> 00:30:58,120
[♪ tense music playing]

552
00:31:05,440 --> 00:31:06,960
Take a look.
Is this the model you're after?

553
00:31:07,480 --> 00:31:10,000
There are four red ones in Istanbul.

554
00:31:10,080 --> 00:31:11,080
Collectable Good Condition

555
00:31:11,160 --> 00:31:12,640
- Exactly. That's the one.
- [laughs]

556
00:31:12,720 --> 00:31:14,440
[horn blaring]

557
00:31:16,840 --> 00:31:17,840
Wow, she's amazing!

558
00:31:17,920 --> 00:31:19,320
Look at the contours.

559
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:22,160
Can you share this with me, Mert?

560
00:31:22,240 --> 00:31:23,240
Sure, I can do that, but...

561
00:31:23,320 --> 00:31:24,760
What are you planning to do with it?

562
00:31:24,840 --> 00:31:25,840
You want to buy it?

563
00:31:27,480 --> 00:31:29,520
No, I'm not buying it. Um...

564
00:31:29,600 --> 00:31:31,080
I'm inquiring for a friend.

565
00:31:31,160 --> 00:31:33,400
- Thanks for finding it.
- [Mert] No sweat.

566
00:31:33,480 --> 00:31:34,840
Meanwhile,

567
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:37,560
my ex got engaged.

568
00:31:38,440 --> 00:31:39,480
You said she'd come back to me.

569
00:31:40,520 --> 00:31:42,000
She will. Be patient.

570
00:31:42,080 --> 00:31:43,240
Share that with me.

571
00:31:43,880 --> 00:31:45,360
I've had enough of waiting.

572
00:31:46,080 --> 00:31:48,120
I think you should give us a chance.

573
00:31:48,200 --> 00:31:50,680
Mert, there's no such thing as "us."
You're still in love with her.

574
00:31:50,760 --> 00:31:53,040
Keep waiting. She'll come back to you.
Share this with me.

575
00:31:53,120 --> 00:31:55,280
This is your polite way
of turning me down.

576
00:31:56,240 --> 00:31:58,440
Thanks, at least you're honest.

577
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:02,280
You're not being a bitch about it.

578
00:32:03,240 --> 00:32:04,800
Um, I wrote in an intimate tone.

579
00:32:04,880 --> 00:32:06,760
So please make sure the boss sees it.

580
00:32:06,840 --> 00:32:09,040
- [Hayal] Nice.
- I'm sure he'll like it.

581
00:32:09,120 --> 00:32:10,400
Me too.

582
00:32:19,920 --> 00:32:22,200
[♪ hopeful music playing]

583
00:32:25,880 --> 00:32:27,800
[Hayal] He turned out to be a writer, too.

584
00:32:27,880 --> 00:32:29,600
Anyway, you take a look at it.

585
00:32:29,680 --> 00:32:30,960
He'll send the rest soon.

586
00:32:31,040 --> 00:32:32,480
He has all our emails.

587
00:32:33,080 --> 00:32:34,480
He's shrewd, though.

588
00:32:34,560 --> 00:32:36,400
He only gave a glimpse.

589
00:32:36,480 --> 00:32:38,320
Anyway, I'll be with the boss.

590
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:42,080
[chuckles]

591
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:44,160
[phone buzzing]

592
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:49,720
Hello?

593
00:32:49,800 --> 00:32:51,320
[Kemal] <i>Are you upset with me?</i>

594
00:32:51,400 --> 00:32:52,720
Where's the rest?

595
00:32:52,800 --> 00:32:55,280
Send it now because people are waiting.

596
00:32:55,360 --> 00:32:57,160
[Kemal]
<i>That's all from me. You have the rest.</i>

597
00:32:57,920 --> 00:33:00,000
<i>You can't hide anymore, Selen.</i>

598
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:02,120
<i>It's time you admit that it's your story.</i>

599
00:33:02,920 --> 00:33:04,440
<i>You know you wanted a chance.</i>

600
00:33:04,520 --> 00:33:06,240
<i>Well, here it is. Grab it.</i>

601
00:33:06,320 --> 00:33:07,680
<i>Tell them about your story.</i>

602
00:33:12,440 --> 00:33:14,440
- [knocks on door]
- Come in.

603
00:33:15,520 --> 00:33:16,840
[Hayal] Aha, Selen.

604
00:33:16,920 --> 00:33:18,760
Come in, take a seat.

605
00:33:18,840 --> 00:33:19,880
So?

606
00:33:20,440 --> 00:33:22,280
Did he send the rest of the story?

607
00:33:23,360 --> 00:33:25,480
The boss thought it was a bit gloomy.

608
00:33:25,560 --> 00:33:26,920
Actually...

609
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:29,680
Well, what she goes through changes her.

610
00:33:29,760 --> 00:33:33,000
It may come across
as a bit fantastical, maybe even mystical.

611
00:33:33,080 --> 00:33:37,840
She's given a sort of gift of foresight.

612
00:33:38,480 --> 00:33:39,480
What do you mean?

613
00:33:39,560 --> 00:33:41,760
Um, like, seeing into the future.

614
00:33:43,640 --> 00:33:45,680
Hmm. [sighs]

615
00:33:45,760 --> 00:33:46,920
Now, I like that.

616
00:33:47,840 --> 00:33:50,080
See how that changes the whole plot?

617
00:33:51,400 --> 00:33:52,480
Tell us more about it.

618
00:33:52,560 --> 00:33:54,760
Are we talking about
some daydream-like state?

619
00:33:54,840 --> 00:33:56,840
- Dreams... She sees it all in her dreams.
- [Hayal] Hmm.

620
00:33:56,920 --> 00:34:00,040
Does she see good or bad things?

621
00:34:00,120 --> 00:34:03,560
Assume she sees stuff,
can she change the course of events?

622
00:34:04,440 --> 00:34:06,120
She sees both the good and the bad.

623
00:34:06,200 --> 00:34:11,640
She can change the course,
but not like a superhero.

624
00:34:13,440 --> 00:34:14,640
This is how it works.

625
00:34:14,720 --> 00:34:16,400
I'll wrap it up.

626
00:34:17,080 --> 00:34:20,480
Yes, she sees the people
she needs to help in her dreams,

627
00:34:20,560 --> 00:34:24,360
and her path ultimately crosses theirs.

628
00:34:24,440 --> 00:34:27,120
She doesn't need to wait
or search for them.

629
00:34:27,200 --> 00:34:29,360
It just happens naturally.

630
00:34:29,880 --> 00:34:32,680
The girl does her best
to change the course of events.

631
00:34:33,280 --> 00:34:38,240
So she prevents an accident,
a disease, or death?

632
00:34:39,200 --> 00:34:41,920
Is that how it works?

633
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:43,400
- Exactly.
- [boss] Hmm.

634
00:34:45,800 --> 00:34:47,000
Nice.

635
00:34:49,400 --> 00:34:50,720
What next?

636
00:34:50,800 --> 00:34:51,880
Where's the twist?

637
00:34:52,880 --> 00:34:53,880
Um...

638
00:34:55,200 --> 00:34:59,240
One day, she sees herself in a dream
for the first time.

639
00:34:59,320 --> 00:35:00,720
She actually sees her own death.

640
00:35:04,720 --> 00:35:05,920
That's all for now.

641
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:07,240
This is as far as I got.

642
00:35:07,320 --> 00:35:08,320
There's nothing more.

643
00:35:09,800 --> 00:35:11,840
What? Is he going to send them
as chapters?

644
00:35:11,920 --> 00:35:14,480
She probably saves herself. Of course...

645
00:35:16,280 --> 00:35:17,280
I hope.

646
00:35:17,360 --> 00:35:19,480
So, didn't Kemal send the rest?

647
00:35:19,560 --> 00:35:21,000
Come on, why don't we read the email?

648
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:23,440
Kemal sent me nothing.

649
00:35:30,200 --> 00:35:31,400
This is my story.

650
00:35:32,320 --> 00:35:34,080
The story of my film.

651
00:35:39,720 --> 00:35:40,720
[laughs]

652
00:35:41,720 --> 00:35:43,360
- Hand me your glass.
- [gasps]

653
00:35:49,800 --> 00:35:50,880
To your movie.

654
00:35:53,560 --> 00:35:55,880
A special thanks for your kind gesture.

655
00:35:57,200 --> 00:35:59,160
Tell me all about it. How did it go?

656
00:36:02,520 --> 00:36:04,320
You wouldn't believe it.

657
00:36:04,400 --> 00:36:05,520
My knees were shaking.

658
00:36:05,600 --> 00:36:07,120
It was so tough for me.

659
00:36:07,200 --> 00:36:08,800
I told them the story was mine.

660
00:36:09,400 --> 00:36:11,720
I still don't know how I said it.

661
00:36:12,760 --> 00:36:13,880
They were in shock.

662
00:36:13,960 --> 00:36:15,880
- You should have seen Hayal.
- [chuckles]

663
00:36:15,960 --> 00:36:17,280
Then came all the questions.

664
00:36:17,360 --> 00:36:20,080
"Why did you wait?"
"Why didn't you tell us?"

665
00:36:24,720 --> 00:36:26,280
Thank you so much.

666
00:36:26,360 --> 00:36:28,080
I'll never forget this favor.

667
00:36:28,160 --> 00:36:29,960
Don't be silly. It's nothing.

668
00:36:30,040 --> 00:36:31,160
Forget about it.

669
00:36:32,440 --> 00:36:35,080
Tell me the rest of the story.
That's all I want.

670
00:36:36,200 --> 00:36:38,000
You're so persistent.

671
00:36:38,080 --> 00:36:40,320
I'm curious. Is that really so strange?

672
00:36:40,400 --> 00:36:42,680
You decided to marry her off
to a senile man.

673
00:36:42,760 --> 00:36:44,600
That's where we left off. So?

674
00:36:46,440 --> 00:36:48,440
[♪ melancholy music playing]

675
00:36:53,080 --> 00:36:56,200
So, they dress Kavin up
and take her to the wedding,

676
00:36:56,280 --> 00:36:58,800
but they never tell her it's her wedding.

677
00:36:58,880 --> 00:37:01,880
She only realizes
when she arrives at the venue.

678
00:37:03,200 --> 00:37:04,360
Unbelievable.

679
00:37:05,200 --> 00:37:06,840
This is such a vile thing to do.

680
00:37:08,360 --> 00:37:10,160
How can stuff like this still happen?

681
00:37:11,240 --> 00:37:12,240
Anyway, don't mind me.

682
00:37:12,320 --> 00:37:14,400
Please go on. So? I'm listening.

683
00:37:14,480 --> 00:37:20,000
Well, they get married, but the girl
runs away before consummation.

684
00:37:20,080 --> 00:37:21,520
She escapes.

685
00:37:21,600 --> 00:37:23,200
Of course, blood is spilled.

686
00:37:25,720 --> 00:37:29,560
- [sighs]
- The man stabs the girl in the stomach,

687
00:37:29,640 --> 00:37:33,000
but she still escapes
and leaves the village.

688
00:37:36,120 --> 00:37:39,200
I have to admit,
I'm impressed by her determination.

689
00:37:39,280 --> 00:37:41,840
Clearly, it's a rough turn of events, but...

690
00:37:41,920 --> 00:37:45,600
life should give this girl
some kind of gift.

691
00:37:46,680 --> 00:37:48,160
Well, you never really know.

692
00:37:48,240 --> 00:37:50,160
A gift can be a blessing or a curse.

693
00:37:51,840 --> 00:37:53,280
Then what?

694
00:37:53,360 --> 00:37:54,600
Does she make it?

695
00:37:54,680 --> 00:37:56,680
Please tell me she reaches safety.

696
00:37:57,280 --> 00:37:58,320
[sighs]

697
00:37:58,400 --> 00:38:04,240
She hits the road, eventually reaches
Istanbul, and settles into an orphanage.

698
00:38:05,280 --> 00:38:08,120
But she won't reveal
anything about herself.

699
00:38:08,200 --> 00:38:11,480
Not where she's from,
who she is, or her name.

700
00:38:11,560 --> 00:38:12,720
She won't say a word.

701
00:38:12,800 --> 00:38:15,240
- She's silent.
- She won't speak at all?

702
00:38:16,360 --> 00:38:20,520
No, she won't,
because revealing anything about her past

703
00:38:20,600 --> 00:38:24,960
would mean returning to
her previous, hellish life.

704
00:38:25,040 --> 00:38:26,800
What about her family?

705
00:38:26,880 --> 00:38:28,160
Aren't they looking for her?

706
00:38:29,640 --> 00:38:32,680
I doubt these people would organize
a search party for a girl on the run.

707
00:38:37,160 --> 00:38:41,240
She is given a new name at the orphanage.

708
00:38:41,320 --> 00:38:45,200
A new life. So on and so forth.

709
00:38:49,160 --> 00:38:50,520
What did they call her?

710
00:38:50,600 --> 00:38:52,760
I don't know yet.
I'll come up with a name.

711
00:38:55,160 --> 00:38:56,160
Selen?

712
00:39:00,240 --> 00:39:01,840
No, of course not.

713
00:39:03,840 --> 00:39:04,880
I mean...

714
00:39:04,960 --> 00:39:09,760
I'm not a megalomaniac obsessed
with putting my name in my script.

715
00:39:09,840 --> 00:39:11,440
That's what I meant.

716
00:39:12,720 --> 00:39:14,720
[thunder rumbling]

717
00:39:18,280 --> 00:39:19,520
Is that rain coming?

718
00:39:22,840 --> 00:39:24,840
[thunder continues]

719
00:39:25,720 --> 00:39:27,240
- Captain.
- [captain] Yeah.

720
00:39:27,880 --> 00:39:28,880
Let's head back.

721
00:39:29,600 --> 00:39:30,600
[captain] Okay.

722
00:39:53,680 --> 00:39:54,680
[Selen exclaims]

723
00:39:55,720 --> 00:39:58,520
Rain wasn't expected today. [pants]

724
00:39:58,600 --> 00:40:00,920
- See you. [pants]
- [thunder rumbling]

725
00:40:02,320 --> 00:40:03,320
[Kemal] Selen!

726
00:40:03,400 --> 00:40:07,120
Will she make a friend
over at the orphanage?

727
00:40:09,360 --> 00:40:10,440
I don't know.

728
00:40:11,680 --> 00:40:14,560
I think she should.

729
00:40:16,120 --> 00:40:17,760
Someone she can confide in.

730
00:40:18,800 --> 00:40:21,440
Someone she trusts enough
to share her real name.

731
00:40:21,520 --> 00:40:23,600
Of course, you think it over.

732
00:40:23,680 --> 00:40:25,040
Mine is just an idea.

733
00:40:25,920 --> 00:40:27,640
Not that I know anything about this stuff.

734
00:40:27,720 --> 00:40:29,800
Think about it.

735
00:40:31,200 --> 00:40:34,480
Someone as hurt as her, in every way.

736
00:40:34,560 --> 00:40:36,560
[♪ romantic music playing]

737
00:40:36,640 --> 00:40:38,240
Think... Think of a guy, for example.

738
00:40:39,840 --> 00:40:41,320
They are about the same age.

739
00:40:42,320 --> 00:40:43,760
His father is an alcoholic.

740
00:40:44,560 --> 00:40:48,280
One night,
for no clear reason, he kills his wife.

741
00:40:48,360 --> 00:40:49,960
The kid witnesses it all.

742
00:40:51,760 --> 00:40:53,960
Then, without remorse, he shoots the boy.

743
00:40:56,520 --> 00:40:58,480
Here... He shoots him right here.

744
00:40:58,560 --> 00:40:59,640
His own son.

745
00:41:01,840 --> 00:41:03,880
Believing the boy is dead,
he commits suicide.

746
00:41:06,200 --> 00:41:07,640
But the boy survives.

747
00:41:08,280 --> 00:41:09,600
He stays in hospital for months.

748
00:41:09,680 --> 00:41:10,880
He somehow makes it.

749
00:41:12,120 --> 00:41:15,080
He clings to life,
not knowing what he is fighting for.

750
00:41:17,560 --> 00:41:19,800
Don't you think they'd be good together?

751
00:41:22,920 --> 00:41:24,720
They hold on to each other.

752
00:41:24,800 --> 00:41:27,880
The girl finally finds
someone who believes in her.

753
00:41:27,960 --> 00:41:28,960
She trusts him.

754
00:41:31,520 --> 00:41:33,760
Of course, she doesn't leave the guy.

755
00:41:33,840 --> 00:41:35,960
She becomes the joy of his life.

756
00:42:46,360 --> 00:42:47,640
You're shivering.

757
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:52,280
I'm a little scared.

758
00:42:55,920 --> 00:42:57,800
I don't know who hurt you so deeply, but...

759
00:42:59,800 --> 00:43:01,680
I'm not going to be like them.

760
00:44:09,600 --> 00:44:10,600
[grunts]

761
00:44:16,040 --> 00:44:17,040
[chuckles]

762
00:44:20,360 --> 00:44:21,520
Morning.

763
00:44:21,600 --> 00:44:22,880
Morning.

764
00:44:25,680 --> 00:44:26,800
[kisses]

765
00:44:28,560 --> 00:44:29,560
Wake up.

766
00:44:29,640 --> 00:44:31,160
I'm taking you out for breakfast.

767
00:44:31,240 --> 00:44:33,120
It's a great spot. Come on.

768
00:44:33,200 --> 00:44:34,200
[sighs]

769
00:44:55,640 --> 00:44:59,920
[crowd] Ten, nine, eight, seven, six,

770
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:05,040
five, four, three, two, one...

771
00:45:05,120 --> 00:45:07,120
[♪ tense music playing]

772
00:45:23,640 --> 00:45:27,760
Eat whatever you want.
Omelets, toasted sandwiches, turnovers.

773
00:45:27,840 --> 00:45:29,880
Just avoid the scrambled eggs
with tomato. Okay?

774
00:45:31,440 --> 00:45:32,920
What's wrong with this? Aha.

775
00:45:34,160 --> 00:45:35,160
[sighs]

776
00:45:36,520 --> 00:45:37,520
Come.

777
00:45:39,200 --> 00:45:41,400
- Muhsin.
- [Muhsin] Where have you been, man?

778
00:45:41,480 --> 00:45:43,520
Here I am.
I'm right here. I was busy filming.

779
00:45:43,600 --> 00:45:45,640
- We just finished. What's up?
- Done filming?

780
00:45:45,720 --> 00:45:47,120
- Yeah, yeah. Season final.
- Finished?

781
00:45:47,200 --> 00:45:48,880
- Oh, good.
- [Kemal] Selen!

782
00:45:53,480 --> 00:45:54,480
Come.

783
00:45:55,280 --> 00:45:56,680
Um, Selen.

784
00:45:57,200 --> 00:45:58,760
- Hello.
- Muhsin. He owns the café.

785
00:45:58,840 --> 00:46:00,240
Hello, pleased to meet you.

786
00:46:00,320 --> 00:46:01,600
Me too.

787
00:46:01,680 --> 00:46:03,120
What a nice place.

788
00:46:03,800 --> 00:46:04,920
It sure is.

789
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:06,400
[speaks indistinctly]

790
00:46:06,480 --> 00:46:07,880
- Yeah, it was good.
- Was it?

791
00:46:07,960 --> 00:46:09,520
- I was in the air. Literally.
- Really?

792
00:46:09,600 --> 00:46:10,920
I really was. You...

793
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:12,840
I'll be gone briefly, but I'll be back.

794
00:46:12,920 --> 00:46:14,320
[Muhsin] Emre is asking about you.

795
00:46:14,400 --> 00:46:16,080
- So is Nihal.
- [Kemal] I'm around, man.

796
00:46:16,160 --> 00:46:17,160
You know how it is.

797
00:46:17,240 --> 00:46:19,000
[Muhsin]
You could at least give me a call.

798
00:46:19,080 --> 00:46:20,720
[♪ tense music playing]

799
00:46:20,800 --> 00:46:23,640
[Kemal] I have a phone. Call me anytime.

800
00:46:23,720 --> 00:46:26,000
You should try to get out
of this place now and then.

801
00:46:26,080 --> 00:46:28,480
- How could I, man? How could I leave?
- You've gotten old in here.

802
00:46:28,560 --> 00:46:30,520
You're in nearly all of these.

803
00:46:30,600 --> 00:46:31,720
Well, he's a regular.

804
00:46:31,800 --> 00:46:33,480
And a former employee.

805
00:46:34,360 --> 00:46:35,400
In the kitchen.

806
00:46:36,880 --> 00:46:39,040
You were here on New Year's Eve.

807
00:46:39,120 --> 00:46:40,760
For the last decade.

808
00:46:40,840 --> 00:46:43,800
He won't be this year because he
now has an apartment with a terrace.

809
00:46:43,880 --> 00:46:45,040
That's not true.

810
00:46:45,120 --> 00:46:46,320
You're ditching us.

811
00:46:46,400 --> 00:46:47,960
[Kemal] Geez, man. Fine.

812
00:46:48,040 --> 00:46:49,400
I'll be here on New Year's.

813
00:46:49,480 --> 00:46:50,840
I'll ring in 2026 here, okay?

814
00:46:50,920 --> 00:46:54,360
I promise I'll be here for the countdown.

815
00:46:54,440 --> 00:46:55,800
[Muhsin] We'll see.

816
00:46:55,880 --> 00:46:56,960
We will, won't we?

817
00:46:57,840 --> 00:46:59,560
- Sure.
- See.

818
00:47:01,040 --> 00:47:03,200
What were we having,
scrambled eggs with tomato?

819
00:47:03,280 --> 00:47:04,720
Right away.

820
00:47:04,800 --> 00:47:06,120
You go and take a seat.

821
00:47:06,200 --> 00:47:07,360
Okay.

822
00:47:08,000 --> 00:47:09,120
- [clears throat]
- Make an effort at least.

823
00:47:09,200 --> 00:47:10,240
[sighs]

824
00:47:11,200 --> 00:47:13,480
Bon appétit.

825
00:47:13,560 --> 00:47:15,520
- Thank you.
- [Kemal] Looks so good.

826
00:47:15,600 --> 00:47:17,360
Really. Unbelievable.

827
00:47:18,520 --> 00:47:19,560
[Selen clears throat]

828
00:47:19,640 --> 00:47:21,800
- Don't do that.
- [Kemal] Taste it.

829
00:47:21,880 --> 00:47:23,160
You'll see what I mean.

830
00:47:23,760 --> 00:47:25,360
Be careful, don't burn your mouth.

831
00:47:25,440 --> 00:47:26,480
[Selen] Uh-huh.

832
00:47:29,400 --> 00:47:30,640
It's good. Not bad.

833
00:47:32,640 --> 00:47:34,640
[phone ringing]

834
00:47:36,160 --> 00:47:38,040
- [phone beeps]
- Yes?

835
00:47:39,080 --> 00:47:40,480
Yeah, yeah, I'm at the café.

836
00:47:40,560 --> 00:47:42,480
Um, yes. Okay, come here.

837
00:47:42,560 --> 00:47:43,560
I'm on my way.

838
00:47:44,520 --> 00:47:46,000
Come with me. It'll be quick.
I want to show you something.

839
00:47:46,080 --> 00:47:47,560
- Where to?
- [Kemal] Come, come, come.

840
00:47:47,640 --> 00:47:48,960
That needs to cool down anyway.

841
00:47:54,720 --> 00:47:57,440
- Hasan. Hey! Oh.
- [Hasan] Hello.

842
00:47:57,520 --> 00:47:58,520
Welcome.

843
00:48:01,840 --> 00:48:02,840
[Kemal] It's a monster, huh?

844
00:48:02,920 --> 00:48:04,680
[Hasan] Yeah, it's a good ride.

845
00:48:05,320 --> 00:48:07,040
A private import.

846
00:48:07,120 --> 00:48:09,160
[♪ tense music playing]

847
00:48:14,800 --> 00:48:16,880
Really unique, a special car.

848
00:48:17,760 --> 00:48:19,560
We got it from its second owner.

849
00:48:21,080 --> 00:48:22,080
You've done him good.

850
00:48:22,160 --> 00:48:23,920
- You've also brought him luck.
- [sighs]

851
00:48:25,160 --> 00:48:26,520
It's been his dream for years.

852
00:48:33,160 --> 00:48:34,280
Fuck!

853
00:48:36,200 --> 00:48:37,360
[Muhsin] So when do we celebrate?

854
00:48:37,440 --> 00:48:39,040
Not yet, man.
I only made the down payment.

855
00:48:39,120 --> 00:48:41,880
- Monday, right?
- Yeah, hopefully Monday.

856
00:48:41,960 --> 00:48:42,960
[Kemal] Come on, hop in.

857
00:48:43,040 --> 00:48:45,600
No... Not you, please, man. Selen.

858
00:48:46,760 --> 00:48:48,120
Come on, Selen.

859
00:48:48,880 --> 00:48:50,960
Come, hop in. Come on.

860
00:49:00,360 --> 00:49:01,560
What do you think? You like it, right?

861
00:49:01,640 --> 00:49:03,480
- Good.
- Yes. [sighs]

862
00:49:04,600 --> 00:49:06,080
Do... Do you plan to buy it?

863
00:49:06,840 --> 00:49:08,880
I pretty much did. I mean, we shook hands.

864
00:49:08,960 --> 00:49:14,120
The repairs and maintenance will be steep,
but this is what you get for the money.

865
00:49:14,200 --> 00:49:15,440
[chuckles]

866
00:49:15,520 --> 00:49:21,440
Ma'am, would you consider
taking a long trip with me in this car?

867
00:49:23,680 --> 00:49:25,080
[chuckles, sighs]

868
00:49:25,960 --> 00:49:27,240
I'm working.

869
00:49:27,320 --> 00:49:28,480
How could I?

870
00:49:29,200 --> 00:49:30,560
How come? The season has wrapped up.

871
00:49:31,280 --> 00:49:32,520
Are you still busy?

872
00:49:33,960 --> 00:49:36,200
Well... I don't know.

873
00:49:37,240 --> 00:49:38,880
Selen, is something wrong?

874
00:49:38,960 --> 00:49:42,960
I just got a message.
Um, I realize I made a mistake.

875
00:49:43,040 --> 00:49:47,080
Actually, I forgot about it,
and it's pretty important.

876
00:49:47,160 --> 00:49:48,760
May I leave? [breathes shakily]

877
00:49:48,840 --> 00:49:50,440
I'm really sorry, but it's urgent.

878
00:49:50,520 --> 00:49:53,640
Okay. Okay, but... We haven't...

879
00:49:55,920 --> 00:49:57,480
We haven't finished our breakfast yet.

880
00:49:57,560 --> 00:49:59,960
It's really urgent, honestly. I'm sorry.

881
00:50:15,480 --> 00:50:18,240
Oh! You've got ice cream
everywhere. [chuckles]

882
00:50:18,320 --> 00:50:20,320
[♪ melancholy music playing]

883
00:50:28,360 --> 00:50:30,360
[breathing shakily]

884
00:50:34,920 --> 00:50:36,800
<i>I need to change this.</i>

885
00:50:37,440 --> 00:50:38,640
<i>I need to break free.</i>

886
00:50:38,720 --> 00:50:41,480
[breathing heavily]
<i>I changed other people's destinies.</i>

887
00:50:41,560 --> 00:50:43,440
<i>I must do the same for myself.</i>

888
00:50:50,640 --> 00:50:54,880
198 DAYS

889
00:51:01,560 --> 00:51:03,560
[breathing shakily]

890
00:51:20,040 --> 00:51:21,040
[phone beeps]

891
00:51:27,760 --> 00:51:30,200
- [sighs]
- [Kemal] <i>I would love to see</i>

892
00:51:30,280 --> 00:51:31,280
<i>the Fethiye-Göcek area.</i>

893
00:51:31,360 --> 00:51:34,920
<i>But if you prefer,
we can also go to Çesme or Kas, even.</i>

894
00:51:35,000 --> 00:51:36,720
<i>Kemal, we need you. The set is ready.</i>

895
00:51:36,800 --> 00:51:38,840
<i>Okay, I'm coming. As I was saying, Çesme...</i>

896
00:51:38,920 --> 00:51:41,640
<i>You tell me where you want to go.</i>

897
00:51:41,720 --> 00:51:45,520
- <i>I'll make all the arrangements.</i> [kisses]
- [phone beeps]

898
00:51:50,200 --> 00:51:51,240
[sighs]

899
00:51:56,600 --> 00:51:57,600
[sighs]

900
00:51:59,400 --> 00:52:00,560
[coworker 1] Morning.

901
00:52:00,640 --> 00:52:02,680
Selen, I heard you're going to
write a script. Congratulations.

902
00:52:11,040 --> 00:52:13,320
Remember the cars we checked out
last week?

903
00:52:13,400 --> 00:52:15,400
I found one for sale.
We have to buy it now.

904
00:52:15,480 --> 00:52:17,440
This is all the money I have.

905
00:52:17,520 --> 00:52:20,080
Um, first of all, good morning to you.
Secondly, what's the matter with you?

906
00:52:20,160 --> 00:52:22,680
Mert, please, I really don't have time.

907
00:52:22,760 --> 00:52:26,000
I need your help,
but we can't buy it in my name.

908
00:52:26,080 --> 00:52:27,520
It has to be registered to someone else.

909
00:52:27,600 --> 00:52:29,120
Um, can you calm down?

910
00:52:29,200 --> 00:52:31,400
I can't because this is
a matter of life and death.

911
00:52:31,920 --> 00:52:32,920
We must buy it.

912
00:52:33,000 --> 00:52:35,280
I need to buy that car
before someone else does.

913
00:52:35,360 --> 00:52:37,520
[♪ tense music playing]

914
00:52:44,240 --> 00:52:45,480
[breathing heavily]

915
00:52:48,800 --> 00:52:51,000
[Mert] <i>Um, Selen.
I had to rush out for something urgent.</i>

916
00:52:51,080 --> 00:52:53,440
<i>I saw that you had already left.</i>

917
00:52:53,520 --> 00:52:55,080
<i>The keys are in the hallway.</i>

918
00:52:55,160 --> 00:52:58,840
<i>The guy was a tough bargainer,
but you know how money can change things.</i>

919
00:52:58,920 --> 00:53:03,480
<i>He ditched the potential buyer
as soon as he saw the cash.</i>

920
00:53:03,560 --> 00:53:05,520
[Selen]
Thanks so much for helping out, Mert.

921
00:53:05,600 --> 00:53:06,600
[Mert] <i>No problem, Selen.</i>

922
00:53:06,680 --> 00:53:07,960
<i>It was a pleasure.</i>

923
00:53:42,360 --> 00:53:46,800
SPIRAL OF SILENCE - FEATURE FILM
STORY & SCREENPLAY - SELEN KAYA

924
00:54:18,160 --> 00:54:20,040
[Kemal] <i>This urgent job of yours
is dragging on.</i>

925
00:54:20,120 --> 00:54:21,960
<i>I was worried about you.</i>

926
00:54:22,040 --> 00:54:23,080
<i>Are you okay?</i>

927
00:54:24,840 --> 00:54:26,280
Fine. You?

928
00:54:26,360 --> 00:54:28,480
[Kemal] <i>I couldn't get the car.
The guy returned my money.</i>

929
00:54:28,560 --> 00:54:29,720
<i>I don't know why. It beats me.</i>

930
00:54:29,800 --> 00:54:31,680
<i>He said he changed his mind or something.</i>

931
00:54:31,760 --> 00:54:33,400
<i>Don't worry about it. It's over now.</i>

932
00:54:33,480 --> 00:54:36,000
<i>I was thinking,
since we still have the money,</i>

933
00:54:36,080 --> 00:54:37,920
<i>maybe we could take a longer vacation.</i>

934
00:54:38,000 --> 00:54:39,560
<i>You're coming with me, right?</i>

935
00:54:40,080 --> 00:54:41,080
Yes, I am.

936
00:55:00,440 --> 00:55:02,040
[hotel clerk] <i>I'm calling from Ada Hotel.</i>

937
00:55:02,120 --> 00:55:03,360
<i>Your payment wasn't received.</i>

938
00:55:03,440 --> 00:55:05,840
<i>Your New Year's reservation
will be canceled.</i>

939
00:55:05,920 --> 00:55:07,160
Yes, I'd like to cancel.

940
00:55:07,240 --> 00:55:08,400
- I'm not coming.
- <i>Okay.</i>

941
00:55:08,480 --> 00:55:11,200
- <i>We'll cancel your reservation. Thank you.</i>
- [phone beeps]

942
00:55:16,120 --> 00:55:17,120
[sighs]

943
00:55:29,080 --> 00:55:30,080
[sighs]

944
00:55:33,600 --> 00:55:35,720
[♪ upbeat music playing]

945
00:55:47,480 --> 00:55:49,760
DON QUIXOTE 2

946
00:55:49,840 --> 00:55:52,480
Hey, do you plan to lie down all day?

947
00:55:54,200 --> 00:55:55,680
What else do you do on vacation?

948
00:55:56,880 --> 00:55:57,960
Here, this is for you.

949
00:56:00,520 --> 00:56:01,520
[sighs]

950
00:56:03,320 --> 00:56:05,040
What if I told you I can't swim?

951
00:56:05,680 --> 00:56:08,080
Oh. Seriously?

952
00:56:09,920 --> 00:56:12,680
Then lesson one will be swimming.

953
00:56:13,720 --> 00:56:14,840
Come on.

954
00:56:14,920 --> 00:56:17,160
- Do I have to?
- [Kemal] Yes, you do.

955
00:56:17,240 --> 00:56:19,240
[♪ upbeat music playing]

956
00:56:23,120 --> 00:56:24,120
[grunts]

957
00:56:28,200 --> 00:56:29,320
[shrieks]

958
00:56:31,160 --> 00:56:32,840
[laughs]

959
00:56:33,840 --> 00:56:36,000
- [speaks indistinctly]
- As you move your legs like this...

960
00:56:50,960 --> 00:56:52,880
How did I do?

961
00:56:52,960 --> 00:56:54,920
- I think you did okay.
- Me too.

962
00:56:55,000 --> 00:56:56,920
Let me take a photo of you.

963
00:56:57,000 --> 00:56:58,000
Okay.

964
00:57:00,800 --> 00:57:02,800
[camera shutter clicking]

965
00:57:04,440 --> 00:57:05,680
Is that good?

966
00:57:09,360 --> 00:57:11,000
[camera shutter clicks]

967
00:57:17,720 --> 00:57:19,240
Isn't it amazing?

968
00:57:20,400 --> 00:57:21,400
What?

969
00:57:28,600 --> 00:57:30,200
No way.

970
00:57:30,280 --> 00:57:31,640
Why not?

971
00:57:31,720 --> 00:57:32,880
Never.

972
00:57:36,120 --> 00:57:38,360
- Ugh!
- You wouldn't believe the view from here.

973
00:57:38,440 --> 00:57:41,000
- You know what? I'm not curious at all.
- [chuckles]

974
00:57:41,080 --> 00:57:43,320
I wish you would at least take a peek.

975
00:57:43,400 --> 00:57:44,680
- [Selen] Never.
- Look.

976
00:57:44,760 --> 00:57:47,880
You're missing the most breathtaking
scenery in the world.

977
00:57:47,960 --> 00:57:50,320
[Selen] Oh, how much longer?

978
00:57:51,400 --> 00:57:52,640
- Are you sure?
- I'm sure.

979
00:57:52,720 --> 00:57:53,760
- No. I don't want to.
- Look at me.

980
00:57:53,840 --> 00:57:55,720
- I really don't want to.
- Hear me out.

981
00:57:55,800 --> 00:57:57,800
Have you regretted
anything we've done together so far?

982
00:57:57,880 --> 00:58:00,000
Is this supposed to be a justification?

983
00:58:00,080 --> 00:58:01,400
- [chuckles]
- I really don't want to.

984
00:58:01,480 --> 00:58:03,520
- Don't you trust me? Hmm?
- [sighs]

985
00:58:03,600 --> 00:58:06,120
You're driving me nuts.

986
00:58:06,200 --> 00:58:07,520
I really don't want to.

987
00:58:07,600 --> 00:58:09,640
- You're going to love it. Trust me.
- [sighs]

988
00:58:09,720 --> 00:58:11,800
Don't you think
you're pushing me too much?

989
00:58:11,880 --> 00:58:14,160
- But there's no other way to convince you.
- [breathes heavily]

990
00:58:14,240 --> 00:58:15,360
What can I do? I love you.

991
00:58:15,440 --> 00:58:17,400
I want to share this experience
with you, okay?

992
00:58:17,480 --> 00:58:19,200
- Ugh! I'm going to pass out here.
- [shushes]

993
00:58:19,280 --> 00:58:20,560
- I really am.
- Go on, go ahead.

994
00:58:20,640 --> 00:58:22,680
I'll hold on to you.

995
00:58:22,760 --> 00:58:25,080
- [gasps] Wait, one sec.
- Once I buckle this...

996
00:58:25,160 --> 00:58:26,600
You're good. Clear your mind.

997
00:58:26,680 --> 00:58:28,360
Clear your mind and start running.

998
00:58:28,440 --> 00:58:30,080
Start running when I tell you to.

999
00:58:30,160 --> 00:58:31,400
Where do I run to?

1000
00:58:31,480 --> 00:58:33,720
Run. All you need to do is run.

1001
00:58:33,800 --> 00:58:35,920
Okay. I'm going. Hold on.

1002
00:58:36,000 --> 00:58:37,240
[Kemal] Selen.

1003
00:58:37,320 --> 00:58:39,320
[♪ adventurous music playing]

1004
00:58:40,360 --> 00:58:41,720
[Kemal] Run when I tell you to.

1005
00:58:41,800 --> 00:58:44,240
- Run! Don't look back.
- [Selen speaks indistinctly] ...one sec.

1006
00:58:44,320 --> 00:58:46,720
- Okay. One moment. Wait.
- [Kemal] Whoo-hoo!

1007
00:58:46,800 --> 00:58:48,440
[Selen] Kemal. Kemal!

1008
00:58:48,520 --> 00:58:50,800
- Oh!
- [Kemal] Whoo-hoo-hoo!

1009
00:58:50,880 --> 00:58:52,360
[screams, speaks indistinctly]

1010
00:58:52,440 --> 00:58:56,240
- Selen. Open your eyes, my love.
- This is too high! No! No!

1011
00:58:56,320 --> 00:58:58,440
- Whoo!
- [screaming]

1012
00:58:59,520 --> 00:59:01,000
Hold on!

1013
00:59:01,080 --> 00:59:02,840
I want to get down. Hold on!

1014
00:59:02,920 --> 00:59:05,120
- [Kemal] We're going down anyway.
- [Selen] Oh!

1015
00:59:07,440 --> 00:59:08,960
This is too high.

1016
00:59:09,040 --> 00:59:11,520
Too high, Kemal!

1017
00:59:11,600 --> 00:59:12,800
- [Kemal] I told you.
- Enough!

1018
00:59:12,880 --> 00:59:14,400
- What? [screams]
- Feel the wind.

1019
00:59:14,480 --> 00:59:15,520
Enough!

1020
00:59:16,160 --> 00:59:17,480
Hold on! This is too high!

1021
00:59:17,560 --> 00:59:18,560
I want out.

1022
00:59:18,640 --> 00:59:22,040
- [Kemal] Honey, we're gliding down.
- [Selen panting, shrieking]

1023
00:59:22,760 --> 00:59:24,240
Enjoy the experience.

1024
00:59:24,880 --> 00:59:28,280
[Selen] Ah! I told you, it's too high!

1025
00:59:28,360 --> 00:59:29,640
Ugh! [screams]

1026
00:59:29,720 --> 00:59:32,200
- Are you happy?
- Not right now!

1027
00:59:32,280 --> 00:59:34,360
- [Kemal] Are you happy?
- No! Wait! No! Stop!

1028
00:59:34,440 --> 00:59:37,080
I'll keep asking this question
until you say yes.

1029
00:59:37,160 --> 00:59:38,520
Shut up!

1030
00:59:43,000 --> 00:59:45,000
[♪ "I'm Yours" playing]

1031
01:00:17,160 --> 01:00:20,960
July
171 DAYS

1032
01:00:29,880 --> 01:00:33,040
August
122 DAYS

1033
01:00:38,240 --> 01:00:39,240
Tasty.

1034
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:43,080
- [speaking indistinctly] Everything...
- [Selen laughs]

1035
01:00:45,720 --> 01:00:47,880
September
92 DAYS

1036
01:00:47,960 --> 01:00:49,680
Hold tight. I'm going faster.

1037
01:00:49,760 --> 01:00:51,320
Holding tight.

1038
01:01:13,080 --> 01:01:14,920
October
63 DAYS

1039
01:01:15,000 --> 01:01:16,000
I wonder what he's up to.

1040
01:01:16,080 --> 01:01:17,680
He called us over for something, but...

1041
01:01:17,760 --> 01:01:18,960
- Ümit!
- [Ümit] Yeah?

1042
01:01:19,040 --> 01:01:20,680
Can I have some ice in this?
I changed my mind.

1043
01:01:20,760 --> 01:01:22,880
- [Ümit] Sure.
- Well, warm...

1044
01:01:27,240 --> 01:01:29,000
See that. Look at him.

1045
01:01:29,080 --> 01:01:31,000
The last thing we need.

1046
01:01:31,080 --> 01:01:33,480
Psst. Over here. Turn that down.

1047
01:01:35,000 --> 01:01:36,000
[music stops]

1048
01:01:40,920 --> 01:01:41,960
Friends!

1049
01:01:44,440 --> 01:01:45,560
Friends!

1050
01:01:45,640 --> 01:01:46,800
Friends!

1051
01:01:46,880 --> 01:01:48,680
Friends! Friends!

1052
01:01:48,760 --> 01:01:50,960
[patron] What's this all about?

1053
01:01:52,400 --> 01:01:54,120
Welcome to you all.

1054
01:01:54,200 --> 01:01:55,680
[patron] Yeah.

1055
01:01:55,760 --> 01:01:57,080
Thanks for coming.

1056
01:01:57,160 --> 01:01:59,680
[patron] Cheers!

1057
01:01:59,760 --> 01:02:03,640
- We've got some news for you.
- [patron] What about?

1058
01:02:03,720 --> 01:02:05,880
One is real big news.

1059
01:02:05,960 --> 01:02:07,120
[patron 1] What can it be?

1060
01:02:07,200 --> 01:02:08,680
- It's shocking!
- What is it?

1061
01:02:08,760 --> 01:02:09,880
- What's the shocker?
- I don't know.

1062
01:02:09,960 --> 01:02:15,680
- [patron] I want to know.
- We have no idea how it happened, but...

1063
01:02:16,960 --> 01:02:18,760
She's pregnant.

1064
01:02:18,840 --> 01:02:25,000
[patrons cheering] Way to go!

1065
01:02:25,080 --> 01:02:27,320
- Congratulations.
- [spouse] Thank you.

1066
01:02:27,400 --> 01:02:29,520
[Muhsin] A menopause baby.
A real stray bullet.

1067
01:02:29,600 --> 01:02:31,360
[patron laughs] It happens.

1068
01:02:31,440 --> 01:02:32,680
[Muhsin] Destiny!

1069
01:02:33,520 --> 01:02:35,800
It all happened most unexpectedly.

1070
01:02:35,880 --> 01:02:37,040
[patron] Wonderful!

1071
01:02:37,120 --> 01:02:38,640
Good for you!

1072
01:02:38,720 --> 01:02:39,720
What's more...

1073
01:02:41,120 --> 01:02:44,600
- we decided to move to the countryside.
- [patrons] Oh!

1074
01:02:44,680 --> 01:02:46,000
[patron] What for?

1075
01:02:46,080 --> 01:02:47,480
They're tearing down the building.

1076
01:02:48,520 --> 01:02:51,560
We won't be able
to celebrate New Year's here.

1077
01:02:55,240 --> 01:02:59,640
- [cheers] Yes! Yes!
- [patron] What's wrong with her?

1078
01:02:59,720 --> 01:03:00,920
Geez!

1079
01:03:01,000 --> 01:03:02,000
What makes you so happy?

1080
01:03:02,080 --> 01:03:03,320
- Is she nuts?
- Why is she so happy?

1081
01:03:03,400 --> 01:03:04,680
- [patron 2] Is this a joke?
- Um...

1082
01:03:04,760 --> 01:03:07,680
I mean, a new life, a new baby.

1083
01:03:08,200 --> 01:03:09,360
I'm happy for them.

1084
01:03:09,440 --> 01:03:11,360
[patrons cheering]

1085
01:03:11,440 --> 01:03:13,400
She always surprises. [laughs]

1086
01:03:13,480 --> 01:03:15,000
Congratulations.

1087
01:03:17,040 --> 01:03:18,160
My man!

1088
01:03:21,120 --> 01:03:24,040
I hope the baby looks nothing like Muhsin.

1089
01:03:24,120 --> 01:03:26,440
- [laughs]
- [laughs]

1090
01:03:26,520 --> 01:03:28,840
God forgive me,
but you know, Muhsin isn't...

1091
01:03:28,920 --> 01:03:30,520
- You're horrible.
- Come on.

1092
01:03:34,720 --> 01:03:35,840
[door closes]

1093
01:03:38,160 --> 01:03:40,840
- Where to?
- Upstairs.

1094
01:03:43,800 --> 01:03:45,160
Darn.

1095
01:03:47,680 --> 01:03:50,240
I don't have to face all my fears.

1096
01:03:50,320 --> 01:03:52,000
- We're ticking the list.
- [sighs]

1097
01:03:54,080 --> 01:03:55,400
[Kemal] Okay, fine.

1098
01:03:55,480 --> 01:03:56,480
FIRST FLOOR

1099
01:03:56,560 --> 01:03:57,600
I won't insist.

1100
01:03:58,880 --> 01:04:00,240
I'll let you off this time.

1101
01:04:02,360 --> 01:04:03,920
- [elevator bell dings]
- See you upstairs.

1102
01:04:09,880 --> 01:04:12,440
Ugh. I've really had enough.

1103
01:04:16,000 --> 01:04:17,280
This is the worst.

1104
01:04:18,360 --> 01:04:19,800
Come.

1105
01:04:21,480 --> 01:04:23,400
- Wait.
- [Kemal] Slowly.

1106
01:04:23,480 --> 01:04:24,640
[Selen] Hold on.

1107
01:04:24,720 --> 01:04:29,240
- Wait. Wait. It's so cramped.
- [clicks tongue]

1108
01:04:29,320 --> 01:04:32,760
- No. It's too small. I can't do it.
- [shushes] It's okay, Selen. Calm down.

1109
01:04:33,400 --> 01:04:35,360
- Easy does it. It's all right.
- What's the matter?

1110
01:04:35,440 --> 01:04:36,480
Look at me, okay? Selen, look at me.

1111
01:04:36,560 --> 01:04:38,000
- Okay, wait. Hold on.
- You're okay.

1112
01:04:38,080 --> 01:04:39,600
- Hold on, wait.
- Keep your eyes on me.

1113
01:04:39,680 --> 01:04:42,840
- Selen. Selen, my dear. I'm with you.
- Wait. What happened? Hold on.

1114
01:04:42,920 --> 01:04:45,040
- Hold on. Oh! Wait, wait.
- Honey, I'm here. I'm here.

1115
01:04:45,120 --> 01:04:46,840
[breathes shakily] Oh, Kemal!

1116
01:04:46,920 --> 01:04:49,560
- Selen. Selen, open your eyes.
- It's so small in here.

1117
01:04:49,640 --> 01:04:50,960
- I can't.
- Open them.

1118
01:04:51,040 --> 01:04:53,480
- Uh-uh. I can't.
- [chuckles] Then you can't see.

1119
01:04:53,560 --> 01:04:55,480
See what exactly?

1120
01:04:55,560 --> 01:04:58,440
- Oh. [sighs]
- [Kemal] You'll see if you look.

1121
01:04:58,520 --> 01:04:59,760
[Selen] See what?

1122
01:04:59,840 --> 01:05:01,880
[♪ romantic music playing]

1123
01:05:05,120 --> 01:05:06,240
What are you doing, Kemal?

1124
01:05:06,320 --> 01:05:08,160
I'm trying to distract you.

1125
01:05:09,600 --> 01:05:11,960
[chuckles] Will you marry me?

1126
01:05:12,640 --> 01:05:13,720
[chuckles]

1127
01:05:15,360 --> 01:05:16,680
- [elevator bell dings]
- [grunts]

1128
01:05:17,920 --> 01:05:21,480
You... You're really insane.

1129
01:05:23,800 --> 01:05:25,360
You didn't answer.

1130
01:05:31,120 --> 01:05:32,120
[sighs]

1131
01:05:33,360 --> 01:05:34,360
[sighs]

1132
01:05:35,960 --> 01:05:40,200
- Yes. Yes. Yes! [screams]
- Whoo-hoo!

1133
01:05:40,720 --> 01:05:43,240
Uh-oh! What's all this noise so late, son?

1134
01:05:43,320 --> 01:05:45,360
It's okay, Auntie Selma.
We're getting married.

1135
01:05:45,440 --> 01:05:47,960
Oh, it's so nice to be young.

1136
01:05:48,040 --> 01:05:49,040
[laughs]

1137
01:05:49,840 --> 01:05:51,840
[♪ romantic music playing]

1138
01:05:53,320 --> 01:05:54,760
[Kemal sighs]

1139
01:06:01,240 --> 01:06:02,240
[moans]

1140
01:06:31,480 --> 01:06:32,480
[sighs]

1141
01:06:37,040 --> 01:06:39,040
[♪ upbeat music playing]

1142
01:06:45,440 --> 01:06:48,560
So, won't you come up to the terrace?

1143
01:06:48,640 --> 01:06:51,280
Come on, come on, come on.

1144
01:06:52,640 --> 01:06:54,080
Kemal the Lionheart.

1145
01:06:54,160 --> 01:06:55,480
Kemal the Gallant.

1146
01:06:55,560 --> 01:06:58,240
Look at him, tall and noble.

1147
01:06:58,320 --> 01:06:59,720
- What did you give him?
- [chuckles]

1148
01:06:59,800 --> 01:07:00,800
Tell me the truth.

1149
01:07:00,880 --> 01:07:01,880
- [speaks indistinctly]
- Yes.

1150
01:07:01,960 --> 01:07:05,240
- Anyone for a refill?
- You could eat the whole animal.

1151
01:07:05,320 --> 01:07:07,440
- Here. For you.
- How did you know?

1152
01:07:08,360 --> 01:07:09,720
Consider it a wild guess.

1153
01:07:09,800 --> 01:07:12,240
- Good for you. Good for you.
- [Selen] What's up?

1154
01:07:12,320 --> 01:07:13,920
This fat-bellied,

1155
01:07:14,000 --> 01:07:16,000
- old fool is making fun of me.
- That's not true.

1156
01:07:16,080 --> 01:07:18,160
[laughs]

1157
01:07:18,240 --> 01:07:20,680
- Leave my boyfriend alone.
- [mumbles]

1158
01:07:20,760 --> 01:07:22,840
- Come, honey.
- She's talking to you.

1159
01:07:22,920 --> 01:07:23,920
Okay.

1160
01:07:35,080 --> 01:07:37,680
The man who saved me from all my fears.

1161
01:07:37,760 --> 01:07:38,760
[Kemal] Hmm.

1162
01:07:39,920 --> 01:07:41,440
What can I do for you?

1163
01:07:45,680 --> 01:07:50,600
I've got something on my mind, but I'm
not sure if now's the right time or place.

1164
01:07:51,320 --> 01:07:52,880
Want to hear it?

1165
01:07:53,840 --> 01:07:54,840
[chuckles]

1166
01:07:59,400 --> 01:08:01,840
[Kemal] These blocks are being built
on my childhood memories.

1167
01:08:01,920 --> 01:08:04,200
[♪ melancholy music playing]

1168
01:08:04,280 --> 01:08:06,320
Look. Here was the garden
I used to play in.

1169
01:08:10,240 --> 01:08:11,480
I'm not entirely sure,

1170
01:08:12,440 --> 01:08:15,880
but our neighbor Uncle Orhan
lived behind this block.

1171
01:08:15,960 --> 01:08:17,560
The man who saved my life.

1172
01:08:17,640 --> 01:08:20,360
He carried me to the taxi stand.

1173
01:08:21,520 --> 01:08:23,360
Does it feel good to be here?

1174
01:08:23,440 --> 01:08:25,760
No, it doesn't. [sighs]

1175
01:08:26,280 --> 01:08:28,200
I've been avoiding the place.

1176
01:08:28,280 --> 01:08:30,240
I heard it was undergoing gentrification.

1177
01:08:30,320 --> 01:08:32,520
I knew the houses were being torn down.

1178
01:08:32,600 --> 01:08:33,800
It was bugging me.

1179
01:08:33,880 --> 01:08:35,800
I wanted to come, but...

1180
01:08:37,120 --> 01:08:38,840
I guess I never found the courage.

1181
01:08:39,360 --> 01:08:40,560
This is the first time.

1182
01:08:42,800 --> 01:08:44,960
I would never have come without you.

1183
01:08:54,720 --> 01:08:57,360
Actually, I didn't bring you here
to give you a tour.

1184
01:08:57,440 --> 01:08:59,880
We came so that this place sees you.

1185
01:09:01,320 --> 01:09:03,480
Like introducing you to my mom.

1186
01:09:04,080 --> 01:09:05,080
[chuckles]

1187
01:09:05,880 --> 01:09:07,480
Come, let me show you something.

1188
01:09:15,680 --> 01:09:17,200
Are you happy?

1189
01:09:17,280 --> 01:09:18,400
Very.

1190
01:09:20,120 --> 01:09:22,000
Since the day I met you.

1191
01:09:24,320 --> 01:09:26,680
There was a void within me.

1192
01:09:26,760 --> 01:09:28,720
I only realized it existed
when you filled it.

1193
01:09:28,800 --> 01:09:29,800
[chuckles]

1194
01:09:30,720 --> 01:09:34,440
I was asking whether you were happy
to be here, but...

1195
01:09:35,800 --> 01:09:37,680
I like your answer better.

1196
01:09:40,440 --> 01:09:41,720
[fireworks exploding]

1197
01:09:46,480 --> 01:09:47,520
Is it past midnight?

1198
01:09:47,600 --> 01:09:49,160
I think so.

1199
01:09:53,080 --> 01:09:54,520
Happy New Year, my love.

1200
01:09:55,200 --> 01:09:56,880
Happy New Year, my love.

1201
01:09:59,520 --> 01:10:01,520
[♪ melancholy music playing]

1202
01:10:05,160 --> 01:10:06,400
Shall we go?

1203
01:10:06,480 --> 01:10:07,960
Okay.

1204
01:10:10,240 --> 01:10:11,280
[Kemal sighs]

1205
01:10:17,560 --> 01:10:18,640
[screams]

1206
01:10:24,040 --> 01:10:26,160
[gasps]

1207
01:10:26,680 --> 01:10:28,680
[breathing shakily]

1208
01:10:32,640 --> 01:10:33,640
[sighs]

1209
01:10:33,720 --> 01:10:35,720
[♪ melancholy music playing]

1210
01:11:26,400 --> 01:11:28,400
[♪ melancholy music playing]

1211
01:11:38,400 --> 01:11:39,400
Selen?

1212
01:11:40,840 --> 01:11:42,840
[phone ringing]

1213
01:11:53,440 --> 01:11:55,440
[line ringing]

1214
01:12:01,200 --> 01:12:02,200
Selen
Why won't you pick up?

1215
01:12:02,280 --> 01:12:03,400
[Kemal] <i>Selen, where are you?</i>

1216
01:12:03,480 --> 01:12:05,280
<i>Why aren't you answering my calls?</i>

1217
01:12:05,360 --> 01:12:07,160
<i>I don't know what's going on.</i>

1218
01:12:07,240 --> 01:12:08,720
<i>I'm coming to your place.</i>

1219
01:12:08,800 --> 01:12:10,880
<i>Let's meet there, okay? We need to talk.</i>

1220
01:12:19,880 --> 01:12:21,880
[doorbell ringing]

1221
01:12:34,640 --> 01:12:36,640
[phone ringing]

1222
01:12:45,800 --> 01:12:48,000
[Kemal] Hayal, where's Selen?

1223
01:12:48,080 --> 01:12:49,080
She's not in her office.

1224
01:12:49,160 --> 01:12:50,560
She's not at her apartment either.

1225
01:12:50,640 --> 01:12:51,760
I can't reach her.

1226
01:12:51,840 --> 01:12:53,800
- I don't know.
- [Kemal] What do you mean?

1227
01:12:53,880 --> 01:12:55,840
Listen, please tell me
if you know something.

1228
01:12:55,920 --> 01:12:57,280
I don't. She took time off.

1229
01:12:57,360 --> 01:12:58,800
I don't know where she went.

1230
01:12:58,880 --> 01:13:00,320
[Kemal] What?

1231
01:13:00,400 --> 01:13:01,760
Why didn't anyone tell me?

1232
01:13:02,360 --> 01:13:03,360
Can you please call her?

1233
01:13:03,440 --> 01:13:05,120
I've tried a thousand times.
She won't answer.

1234
01:13:05,200 --> 01:13:07,040
I texted her, but she won't reply.

1235
01:13:07,120 --> 01:13:08,440
I don't know what to do.

1236
01:13:08,520 --> 01:13:10,480
[Hayal] She won't pick up my calls either.

1237
01:13:10,560 --> 01:13:11,600
So, what happened?

1238
01:13:11,680 --> 01:13:13,480
Something must have happened.
Do you get it?

1239
01:13:13,560 --> 01:13:15,080
No one just disappears like that.

1240
01:13:15,160 --> 01:13:16,240
You don't simply vanish.

1241
01:13:16,320 --> 01:13:17,840
Something happened, but I don't know what.

1242
01:13:17,920 --> 01:13:19,240
I'm losing my mind over here.

1243
01:13:19,320 --> 01:13:21,000
I'm really freaking out.

1244
01:13:21,080 --> 01:13:23,560
I really can't help you.

1245
01:13:27,040 --> 01:13:28,720
Listen.

1246
01:13:29,320 --> 01:13:31,600
If you hear from her
or find out anything, please call me.

1247
01:13:31,680 --> 01:13:33,000
Please.

1248
01:13:33,520 --> 01:13:35,520
[♪ melancholy music playing]

1249
01:13:46,760 --> 01:13:48,320
This is wrong.

1250
01:13:48,400 --> 01:13:50,040
He's distraught.

1251
01:13:51,000 --> 01:13:52,040
What happened to you guys?

1252
01:13:52,120 --> 01:13:53,960
Weren't you supposed to get married?

1253
01:13:54,880 --> 01:13:55,880
[sighs]

1254
01:13:59,280 --> 01:14:02,400
I mean,
if you're both upset, what's the point?

1255
01:14:02,480 --> 01:14:04,400
You could at least explain it to him.

1256
01:14:04,480 --> 01:14:05,520
Um...

1257
01:14:07,400 --> 01:14:08,600
[sighs]

1258
01:14:08,680 --> 01:14:11,720
These are the reports
on the scripts we received yesterday.

1259
01:14:11,800 --> 01:14:13,920
I will send today's batch
via email later tonight.

1260
01:14:14,000 --> 01:14:17,320
More like before I return to the office.

1261
01:14:17,400 --> 01:14:18,640
And your script?

1262
01:14:19,240 --> 01:14:22,920
You promised to deliver
the revised version within a week.

1263
01:14:23,000 --> 01:14:24,320
There's no script.

1264
01:14:24,400 --> 01:14:25,520
Sorry?

1265
01:14:26,560 --> 01:14:30,360
[sighs] I can't find a conclusion
and I can't change what I find.

1266
01:14:30,440 --> 01:14:33,440
I give up. I can't do it.
I won't do it. [breathes shakily]

1267
01:14:33,520 --> 01:14:36,200
Whatever I do,
I can't save the girl in the finale.

1268
01:14:36,280 --> 01:14:38,400
- I just can't.
- How come?

1269
01:14:39,160 --> 01:14:43,720
You said you were ecstatic,
that this was your lifelong passion.

1270
01:14:43,800 --> 01:14:44,920
What changed?

1271
01:14:47,680 --> 01:14:48,960
Is this it?

1272
01:14:58,240 --> 01:15:00,640
[sighs, sniffles]

1273
01:15:42,640 --> 01:15:44,400
Selen, are you okay? What's wrong?

1274
01:15:44,480 --> 01:15:46,600
I was really worried
when I didn't hear from you.

1275
01:15:46,680 --> 01:15:48,320
I thought something had happened to you.

1276
01:15:50,120 --> 01:15:52,960
Listen, I also stopped
by the office today.

1277
01:15:53,040 --> 01:15:54,200
Hayal...

1278
01:15:55,280 --> 01:15:57,160
Selen, are you avoiding me?

1279
01:15:57,240 --> 01:15:59,640
[♪ melancholy music playing]

1280
01:15:59,720 --> 01:16:01,160
Can we please talk?

1281
01:16:01,680 --> 01:16:03,000
Please.

1282
01:16:23,160 --> 01:16:26,240
[sighs] It's...
It's not working out, Kemal. [sniffles]

1283
01:16:27,520 --> 01:16:29,280
I want to break up.

1284
01:16:33,720 --> 01:16:34,720
Why?

1285
01:16:39,240 --> 01:16:41,080
Selen, you can't keep quiet forever.

1286
01:16:41,160 --> 01:16:42,520
You have to say something.

1287
01:16:44,080 --> 01:16:45,440
There must be a reason.

1288
01:16:47,640 --> 01:16:49,640
I don't know. Was it the idea of marriage
that made you nervous?

1289
01:16:49,720 --> 01:16:51,280
All right, screw it.

1290
01:16:51,360 --> 01:16:52,640
Let's not get married. Forget it.

1291
01:16:55,400 --> 01:16:56,760
And here you are crying.

1292
01:16:56,840 --> 01:16:58,760
That only confuses me more.

1293
01:17:01,320 --> 01:17:02,400
Selen, I beg you.

1294
01:17:02,480 --> 01:17:03,960
What's wrong? What is it?

1295
01:17:04,040 --> 01:17:06,520
You're holding something back from me.

1296
01:17:07,840 --> 01:17:09,520
Was it me? Did I mess up?

1297
01:17:10,440 --> 01:17:13,080
Okay, correct me then.
Fix me. Do whatever it takes.

1298
01:17:13,160 --> 01:17:14,760
We can get through this together.

1299
01:17:15,720 --> 01:17:18,200
But you can't just ghost me like this.

1300
01:17:20,920 --> 01:17:22,680
Don't do this to me.

1301
01:17:24,120 --> 01:17:26,400
Don't leave me wounded like my father.

1302
01:17:26,480 --> 01:17:28,920
I love you so much.

1303
01:17:29,000 --> 01:17:31,200
I will love you until I die.

1304
01:17:31,280 --> 01:17:33,320
Well, I love you too.

1305
01:17:34,000 --> 01:17:37,760
So, what's the problem?

1306
01:17:40,280 --> 01:17:42,880
[sighs, sobs]

1307
01:17:42,960 --> 01:17:44,000
I can't, Kemal.

1308
01:17:44,080 --> 01:17:45,160
Please understand.

1309
01:17:45,240 --> 01:17:46,240
I can't do it.

1310
01:17:47,120 --> 01:17:48,760
It's nothing to do with you.

1311
01:17:48,840 --> 01:17:50,560
It's probably about me.

1312
01:17:50,640 --> 01:17:51,840
I'm the problem.

1313
01:17:51,920 --> 01:17:53,240
What?

1314
01:17:53,320 --> 01:17:55,080
Let's not ruin something so pure.

1315
01:17:55,160 --> 01:17:56,880
Cherish the precious memories.

1316
01:17:56,960 --> 01:17:59,120
Are you trying to drive me crazy?

1317
01:17:59,800 --> 01:18:01,760
Why would we ruin anything?

1318
01:18:01,840 --> 01:18:03,680
[sighs]

1319
01:18:03,760 --> 01:18:04,760
Stop talking nonsense.

1320
01:18:04,840 --> 01:18:07,480
Give me a good reason
and I'll get the fuck out of here.

1321
01:18:07,560 --> 01:18:08,560
Honestly.

1322
01:18:10,400 --> 01:18:11,480
There's no reason.

1323
01:18:11,560 --> 01:18:13,520
There isn't.
There really isn't. [inhales sharply]

1324
01:18:15,160 --> 01:18:16,720
Selen, what are you keeping from me?

1325
01:18:17,760 --> 01:18:19,720
What do you want me to do? Kiss your feet?

1326
01:18:19,800 --> 01:18:21,400
Do you want me to beg you?

1327
01:18:21,480 --> 01:18:26,080
It's nothing. There's
nothing I can say. [sniffles, sobs]

1328
01:18:26,160 --> 01:18:27,280
Go, Kemal.

1329
01:18:27,360 --> 01:18:28,440
It's over.

1330
01:18:28,960 --> 01:18:30,960
[breathing shakily]

1331
01:18:31,680 --> 01:18:33,040
You're running away, right?

1332
01:18:33,120 --> 01:18:34,920
[♪ melancholy music playing]

1333
01:18:35,000 --> 01:18:37,000
I mean, you're giving up.

1334
01:18:40,440 --> 01:18:42,040
What scared you?

1335
01:18:42,880 --> 01:18:44,040
Being happy?

1336
01:18:45,960 --> 01:18:47,480
My love for you?

1337
01:18:54,480 --> 01:18:57,680
[scoffs, sighs]

1338
01:18:57,760 --> 01:18:59,080
Okay, fine.

1339
01:19:04,040 --> 01:19:05,200
What else can I say?

1340
01:19:05,280 --> 01:19:07,160
I hope you find what you're looking for.

1341
01:19:19,080 --> 01:19:20,240
[door opens]

1342
01:19:20,320 --> 01:19:21,840
[door slams]

1343
01:19:21,920 --> 01:19:23,920
[sobbing]

1344
01:19:28,480 --> 01:19:30,520
[sobbing]

1345
